 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Come on under the umbrella with a big box of honey on a plate. Wasps smell the honey and leave you alone. Not if you protect the food. Hide small portions under a tight lid in the cool shadows. They can't get in with jam on top. It does, if you move it every time you see a wasp coming. Wasps remember the spot for days, but they only think it's their own nest. Sorry, one on plate of food. Wasps are gentle around food, they're competing with each other for snacks.",
